348
00:35:19,483 --> 00:35:39,495
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if you're annoyed at people, and say you're kind of stuck with those people for... say you're on, like, a long train, you're... and, like, these people are annoying you, like... unless you're really developed already, like, so long as they're kind of right there, you're gonna be kind of blaming them for it.

349
00:35:39,535 --> 00:35:47,100
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's say something happens, you're annoyed with somebody, and then you're alone in your room for the rest of the day, and that's still kind of...

350
00:35:48,309 --> 00:35:49,630
[SPEAKER_00]: That becomes more obvious.

351
00:35:49,670 --> 00:35:51,051
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, okay, it's me.

352
00:35:51,111 --> 00:35:51,631
[SPEAKER_00]: It's me.

353
00:35:51,651 --> 00:35:56,254
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, I've been alone for 12 hours and here I am still kind of...

354
00:35:56,855 --> 00:36:01,678
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not obvious and that's why, like, this solitude and stuff, it's not like one evening I do it.

355
00:36:01,738 --> 00:36:11,365
[SPEAKER_01]: No, it's a training for a prolonged period of time and then you're kind of putting yourself in the situation where you will be able to discern it if you try.

356
00:36:12,571 --> 00:36:15,455
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, eh... that's exactly what it says.

357
00:36:15,495 --> 00:36:17,418
[SPEAKER_03]: You won't be able to see your signs of your mind.

358
00:36:17,999 --> 00:36:24,928
[SPEAKER_03]: In other words, those internal choices you're making, you won't be able to see that unless you, eh... you train yourself in solitude.

359
00:36:25,869 --> 00:36:26,210
[SPEAKER_03]: So...

360
00:36:27,944 --> 00:36:31,507
[SPEAKER_01]: And obviously, as well, you need to be alone to practice metta.

361
00:36:32,448 --> 00:36:48,861
[SPEAKER_01]: As you said, you cannot be, like I mentioned before, engaging with people, trying to practice loving actions and kind actions and stuff, helping people, and expecting to practice metta, because that's not what it's about.

362
00:36:48,901 --> 00:36:55,346
[SPEAKER_03]: It might make you feel good, but again, it would be in that temporary management sense, and you're not actually discerning.

363
00:36:56,180 --> 00:37:02,245
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you have these intentions of the will that you are liable to externally.

364
00:37:02,425 --> 00:37:14,295
[SPEAKER_01]: And you also want to look at it in a certain way where, like, you know, okay, what I think Metta is, I've been developing it towards this person in these external ways of

365
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:23,744
[SPEAKER_01]: Either through actions, like helping them out, and again, not that that's bad, but the wrong view is thinking that that is where the practice happens.

366
00:37:23,944 --> 00:37:30,847
[SPEAKER_03]: You know, helping them out, and using super gentle, kind speech, and with my mind as well, thinking these loving thoughts.

367
00:37:32,028 --> 00:37:42,193
[SPEAKER_01]: And now, if somebody comes and harms that person, would I have a will towards the person who... like, is that actually increasing

