394
00:39:59,801 --> 00:40:06,664
[SPEAKER_04]: So, if you have a society that tends towards the hedonistic side of the spectrum, that values come for an instant sensual gratification.

395
00:40:06,684 --> 00:40:07,184
[SPEAKER_04]: An accumulation.

396
00:40:07,665 --> 00:40:10,786
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, that is just sowing the seeds for future conflict.

397
00:40:11,506 --> 00:40:15,608
[SPEAKER_04]: And so, that is also a way of seeing the danger in sensuality.

398
00:40:16,249 --> 00:40:22,172
[SPEAKER_04]: And it's important, it seems to me, to not think like black and white, like, oh, rights of peace is not the absence of war.

399
00:40:23,185 --> 00:40:25,846
[SPEAKER_04]: It's also not like that.

400
00:40:25,926 --> 00:40:32,247
[SPEAKER_04]: This is why the Buddha often talks about, you know, or this is why we talk about liability to things.

401
00:40:32,367 --> 00:40:35,268
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you cannot just say something doesn't seem to be happening externally.

402
00:40:35,608 --> 00:40:36,928
[SPEAKER_04]: Therefore, I'm at peace.

403
00:40:36,968 --> 00:40:39,709
[SPEAKER_04]: No, because circumstances change and then the whole thing still explodes.

