444
00:43:23,316 --> 00:43:30,818
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you fill that bowl up, which is the gradual training, the sensory train, virtue, not acting out of these unwholesome intentions.

445
00:43:31,278 --> 00:43:48,424
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, whether you tilt it in the direction of brahmajāras, jhānas, immaterial attainments, casinas, whatever, whatever takes your fancy, it will go in that direction, because all of it revolves around that principle of feeling and craving.

446
00:43:57,285 --> 00:44:01,231
[SPEAKER_03]: If it doesn't revolve around that, then it's not part of the Buddhist teaching, and he wouldn't have mentioned it.

447
00:44:01,712 --> 00:44:08,542
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why he said he teaches only one thing, suffering and freedom from suffering, which is abandoning of craving.

